# Prism live-test credentials: TEMPLATE (names and placeholders only, safe to commit).
#
# Copy it OUTSIDE the repository, never into the checkout. Every assignment
# below is commented out, so a fresh copy enables nothing: uncomment and fill
# only the variables for the suites you intend to run. Every other suite skips
# with a reason. The runners read $PRISM_LIVE_ENV_FILE, else
# ~/.config/prism/live.env.
#
#   install -d -m 700 ~/.config/prism
#   install -m 600 scripts/live.env.example ~/.config/prism/live.env
#   export PRISM_LIVE_ENV_FILE=~/.config/prism/live.env
#
# Add a key without it touching shell history, the terminal, or a chat:
#
#   read -rs HYPER_API_KEY && printf 'HYPER_API_KEY=%s\n' "$HYPER_API_KEY" >> ~/.config/prism/live.env && unset HYPER_API_KEY
#
# Run suites (Bun; the runner loads the file itself, no dotenv dependency):
#
#   bun scripts/live-matrix.mjs --check                          # which suites would run, no spawns
#   PRISM_LIVE_FILTER=providers/hyper bun run test:live          # one suite
#   PRISM_LIVE_STRICT=1 PRISM_LIVE_FILTER=providers/ bun run test:live   # release T1
#
# Release acceptance (tiers, procedure, triage, evidence): docs/live-testing.md,
# "Release acceptance on live providers".
#
# Rules:
# - One least-privilege, spend-capped key per provider. Rotate a key after a
#   suspected leak and after each release run.
# - Keys live in this file only: never in shell rc files or history, never in
#   argv, never in committed files, chat, CI logs, or reports. Suites assert
#   assertNoSecretLeak over everything they produce.
# - The loader accepts KEY=VALUE lines and full-line comments only. Keep
#   comments on their own line: an inline "# ..." becomes part of the value.
# - CI never reads this file. GitHub Environments hold secrets instead
#   (.github/workflows/live-canaries.yml, .github/workflows/live-matrix.yml).

# ── master switches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without its switch a suite family skips even when its keys are present.
# Provider live suites (providers/*), release/journey-*, release/cache-parity:
# PRISM_LIVE_PROVIDER_TESTS=1
# The provider-agnostic SDK journey (release/journey-hyper, release/journey-opencode-go):
# PRISM_LIVE_RELEASE_JOURNEY=1
# Cache parity against pi (release/cache-parity) and the manual provider probe:
# PRISM_LIVE_CACHE_PARITY=1
# Web search and fetch (brave, exa, firecrawl):
# PRISM_LIVE_WEB=1
# Browser live (real Chromium, no key):
# PRISM_LIVE_PLAYWRIGHT=1
# Obscura live (local CLI binary, no key):
# PRISM_LIVE_OBSCURA=1
# Observational-memory live (uses OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY):
# PRISM_LIVE_OBSERVATIONAL_MEMORY_TESTS=1
# LLM compaction live (stub leg):
# PRISM_LIVE_COMPACTION_TESTS=1
# OpenAPI tools against a public spec (no key):
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENAPI_TOOLS=1
# Manual-only release rows:
# PRISM_LIVE_MEMORY_BENCH_MANUAL=1
# PRISM_LIVE_EVAL_GATE_MANUAL=1

# ── release providers (the ten T1 rows that gate 0.13.0) ────────────────────
# Hyper (providers/hyper, release/journey-hyper):
# HYPER_API_KEY=
# OpenCode Go (providers/opencode-go, release/journey-opencode-go):
# OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY=
# TypeSafe / Jev (providers/typesafe):
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Liquid hosted, d1.1 and d1-ultra (providers/liquid):
# LIQUID_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter (providers/openrouter): the pinned free model by default.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Kilo AI Gateway (providers/kilo); :free ids need no credit:
# KILO_API_KEY=
# LiteLLM proxy pool key (providers/litellm); `bun scripts/litellm/up.mjs --write-key` appends it:
# LITELLM_API_KEY=
# Laya (providers/laya): a local laya-serve; no key.
# PRISM_LIVE_LAYA=1
# LAYA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Liquid local (providers/liquid-local): llama-server b11480+ serving d1-3B; no key.
# PRISM_LIVE_LLAMA_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# OpenAI Codex (providers/openai-codex): no key. The Sign in with ChatGPT grant
# lives in the OS keyring (bun scripts/provider-login.mjs --provider openai-codex).
# PRISM_TEST_KEYCHAIN=1
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENAI_CODEX_CREDENTIAL=keyring:openai-codex

# ── OpenRouter paid legs (separately opted in, owner authorization only) ────
# Paid Anthropic cache leg; under $0.05 per run. Off unless set.
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENROUTER_PAID=1
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENROUTER_CACHE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5
# Never openrouter/free or openrouter/auto for a release row.
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENROUTER_MODEL=recursive/flint-v1.0:free

# ── providers that run but do not gate 0.13.0 ───────────────────────────────
# Command Code (providers/commandcode, release/cache-parity, release/skill-evals):
# COMMAND_CODE_API_KEY=
# Ollama Cloud (providers/ollama-cloud, release/cache-parity):
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# ── SDK journey models (release/journey-*) ──────────────────────────────────
# Unset = the manifest default. Pick a tool-capable model, the cheapest that
# passes its provider's T1 tool-loop scenario.
# PRISM_LIVE_HYPER_JOURNEY_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENCODE_GO_JOURNEY_MODEL=

# ── provider model overrides (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Each suite probes the manifest default (scripts/live-matrix.json model[].default)
# unless its variable is set.
# PRISM_LIVE_HYPER_CHAT_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro
# PRISM_LIVE_HYPER_MESSAGES_MODEL=qwen3.6-plus
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENCODE_GO_CHAT_MODEL=mimo-v2.5
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENCODE_GO_MESSAGES_MODEL=qwen3.6-plus
# PRISM_LIVE_TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-latest
# PRISM_LIVE_LAYA_MODEL=laya
# PRISM_LIVE_LIQUID_MODELS=d1.1,d1-ultra
# PRISM_LIVE_LIQUID_LOCAL_MODEL=d1-3B
# PRISM_LIVE_OPENAI_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol
# PRISM_LIVE_KILO_CHAT_MODEL=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it
# PRISM_LIVE_KILO_RESPONSES_MODEL=openai/gpt-6-luna
# PRISM_LIVE_KILO_MESSAGES_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5
# PRISM_LIVE_LITELLM_MODEL=prism-free/gpt-oss-20b@groq
# PRISM_LIVE_COMMANDCODE_CHAT_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash
# PRISM_LIVE_COMMANDCODE_RESPONSES_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# PRISM_LIVE_COMMANDCODE_MESSAGES_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# PRISM_LIVE_OLLAMA_CLOUD_MODEL=gemma4:31b
# PRISM_LIVE_OLLAMA_CLOUD_THINKING_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b

# ── cache parity cells (release/cache-parity) ───────────────────────────────
# PRISM_LIVE_PARITY_COMMANDCODE_CHAT_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash
# PRISM_LIVE_PARITY_COMMANDCODE_RESPONSES_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# PRISM_LIVE_PARITY_COMMANDCODE_MESSAGES_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# PRISM_LIVE_PARITY_OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma4:31b

# ── manual release rows (context rot, skill evals, memory bench, eval gate) ─
# PRISM_LIVE_CONTEXT_ROT_HYPER_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro-0813
# PRISM_LIVE_CONTEXT_ROT_OPENCODE_MODEL=mimo-v2.5
# PRISM_LIVE_SKILL_EVAL_HYPER_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro-0813
# PRISM_LIVE_SKILL_EVAL_OPENCODE_MODEL=mimo-v2.5
# PRISM_LIVE_SKILL_EVAL_OPENROUTER_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free
# PRISM_LIVE_SKILL_EVAL_KILO_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl:free
# PRISM_LIVE_SKILL_EVAL_COMMANDCODE_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.7-Flash
# PRISM_LIVE_MEMORY_BENCH_MODEL=mimo-v2.5
# PRISM_LIVE_EVAL_GATE_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro-0813

# ── LiteLLM free pool backends (scripts/litellm/, local loopback proxy) ─────
# Fill only the backends you want deployed; the rest are dropped from the
# rendered config. Not release evidence.
# Admin key for the local proxy; needed to mint the pool key:
# LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
# PRISM_LIVE_LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
# Groq free tier, 30 RPM / 1000 RPD per model:
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA NIM free tier, about 40 RPM (the pool sets 20):
# NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=
# Google AI Studio free tier, 5 RPM / 20 RPD on Flash; content may train.
# Use a Cloud project with no billing linked: linking billing ends the free tier.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Cloudflare Workers AI free plan:
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=

# ── other vendor keys still named by manifest rows ──────────────────────────
# calibration/vendor-count-tokens (count-only requests):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# PRISM_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# PRISM_LIVE_GOOGLE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# cli/journey (first init-catalog provider key present) and cli/live-journey:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# KIMI_API_KEY=
# ZAI_API_KEY=
# OPENCODE_API_KEY=
# NEURALWATT_API_KEY=
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# ── web tools ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRISM_BRAVE_SEARCH_TOKEN=
# PRISM_EXA_API_KEY=
# PRISM_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# ── messaging channels ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRISM_LIVE_TELEGRAM=1
# Bot token only, never a user account:
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Optional; one notice only, to a chat you operate:
# PRISM_LIVE_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# PRISM_LIVE_SIGNAL=1
# PRISM_LIVE_SIGNAL_SOCKET=/run/signal-cli/socket
# PRISM_LIVE_SIGNAL_ACCOUNT=+15555550100
# PRISM_LIVE_SIGNAL_TERMS_VERSION=2024-01-01
# Optional; one notice only, to a UUID you operate:
# PRISM_LIVE_SIGNAL_RECIPIENT_UUID=

# ── local binaries and services (pointers, no secrets) ──────────────────────
# PRISM_OBSCURA_BIN=/path/to/obscura
# PRISM_TEST_PLAYWRIGHT=1
# PRISM_TEST_LIBREOFFICE=1
# PRISM_TEST_ACP_CLIENT=1
# PRISM_TEST_MCP_CLIENT=1
# PRISM_LIVE_DRAWIO_URL=https://drawio.example/export
# PRISM_TEST_DRAWIO_URL=https://drawio.example/export
# Fill the user and password in your copy only:
# PRISM_TEST_POSTGRES_URL=postgres://<user>:<password>@localhost:5432/prism_test
# PRISM_TEST_NATS_URL=nats://localhost:4222
# PRISM_TEST_DOCKER_SANDBOX=1
# PRISM_TEST_DOCKER_BIN=docker
# PRISM_TEST_DOCKER_IMAGE=<pinned-minimal-image>
# PRISM_TEST_DOCKER_USER=<non-root-user>
# PRISM_TEST_COMPUTER_USE=1
# PRISM_COMPUTER_USE_BIN=/path/to/computer-use-linux
# PRISM_TEST_OPA_URL=https://opa.example:8181/v1/data/prism/allow

# ── RAG rerankers and Drive sync ────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRISM_TEST_TEI_RERANKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081
# PRISM_LIVE_TEI_RERANKER_MODEL=
# PRISM_TEST_HOSTED_RERANK_URL=https://rerank.example/v1/rerank
# PRISM_LIVE_HOSTED_RERANK_MODEL=
# PRISM_TEST_LOCAL_RERANK=1
# PRISM_TEST_LOCAL_RERANK_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/model-cache
# PRISM_LIVE_LOCAL_RERANK_MODEL=Xenova/bge-reranker-base
# Delegated Drive readonly token, one throwaway folder:
# PRISM_TEST_DRIVE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# PRISM_TEST_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=
# PRISM_TEST_DRIVE_SHARED_DRIVE_ID=

# ── hosted sandboxes and OCR (throwaway resources only) ─────────────────────
# PRISM_TEST_E2B_API_KEY=
# PRISM_TEST_MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# ── canaries against DEPLOYED Prism instances (scripts/live-canary.mjs) ─────
# PRISM_LIVE_CANARIES requires every canary variable below together.
# PRISM_LIVE_CANARIES=1
# PRISM_CANARY_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# PRISM_CANARY_REPORT=/path/to/canary-report.json
# PRISM_CANARY_PROVIDER_URL=https://your-prism-provider.example/
# PRISM_CANARY_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# PRISM_CANARY_PROVIDER_MODEL=
# PRISM_CANARY_MCP_URL=https://your-prism-mcp.example/
# PRISM_CANARY_MCP_TOKEN=
# PRISM_CANARY_A2A_URL=https://your-prism-a2a.example/
# PRISM_CANARY_A2A_TOKEN=
